.TH CLRUCACHE_SET_FULL 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
clrucache_set_full \- store a value by key (write-through)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <clrucache.h>

ccol_retval_t clrucache_set_full(clru_cache cache,
                                 const cmap_pair *key_pair,
                                 const cmap_pair *val_pair);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Associates key_pair with val_pair in the cache.

If a remote setter was provided at construction it is called
synchronously outside the mutex before the cache is updated. On
setter failure the function returns ccol_unexpected_failure and the
cache is left unchanged for that key (an existing value is preserved).

Multiple setters for the same key are serialised. Concurrent getters
for the same key block until the set completes.

If the cache is at capacity and the key is new, the least-recently-
used live entry is evicted first.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cache     Cache handle.
key_pair  Key to store (ptr and size fields must be set).
val_pair  Value to associate with the key (ptr and size must be set;
          size must be > 0).
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success             Value stored (and remote setter succeeded if
                         one was provided).
ccol_unexpected_failure  Remote setter returned false; cache unchanged.
ccol_invalid_args        cache, key_pair, or val_pair is NULL; or
                         val_pair->size is 0.
ccol_not_enough_memory   Memory allocation for the new value failed.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
O(1) average-case complexity for the hash map operations.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clru_set (3),
.BR clrucache_get_full (3),
.BR clrucache_create_full (3)
